#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""perihelion-theme: color the desktop to match the wallpaper.

Two styles. Catppuccin (the default) reads the wallpaper, picks a Catppuccin
flavor (Latte, Frappé, Macchiato or Mocha) from how light it is, and three
Catppuccin accents from its strongest colors: every color is a real
Catppuccin color. Material You runs matugen, simpbar's own theming engine, for
Material Design 3 colors made from the wallpaper (its scheme picker: tonal
spot, vibrant, ...). Either way the colors go everywhere the shell draws:

  ~/.config/simpbar/matugen.json        the bar, the cava wave, desktop widgets
  ~/.config/nwg-drawer/drawer.css       the app drawer (Super+A)
  ~/.config/fuzzel/fuzzel.ini [colors]  the launcher and the power menu
  ~/.config/strata/themes/tokyo-night.toml   Strata, the file manager
  ~/.config/mango/colors.conf           Mango's window borders
  ~/.config/fastfetch/config.jsonc      the distro logo, section headers and values
  ~/.config/kitty/perihelion-colors.conf   the terminal itself (live, SIGUSR1)
  ~/.config/cava/config                 terminal cava's gradient (live, SIGUSR2)
  ~/.config/btop/themes/perihelion.theme   btop (btop.conf picks "perihelion")
  ~/.config/perihelion/cmatrix-color    cmatrix's color (Perihelion's wrapper)
  ~/.config/mako/config                 notifications (Mango), reloaded live
  the login screen (SDDM, Pixie)        through perihelion-greeter-sync

and tells simpbar and simpbar-shell to reload (SIGUSR1).

Settings, ~/.config/simpbar/theme (Simpbar Config writes it):
  style=catppuccin   catppuccin (a palette, matched to the wallpaper), or
                     material (Material You, via matugen)
  palette=catppuccin-auto   catppuccin-auto|-latte|-frappe|-macchiato|-mocha,
                     gruvbox-auto|-dark|-light, rose-pine-auto, rose-pine,
                     rose-pine-moon, rose-pine-dawn, nord, tokyo-night
  tint=on            Wallpaper tint: the palette's backgrounds, surfaces and
                     text take a dark shade of the wallpaper's main hue (its
                     lightness steps stay the palette's)
  accent=wallpaper   wallpaper (the palette's accents nearest the image's
                     colors) or flavor (the palette's own defaults)
  scheme=scheme-tonal-spot   Material You: matugen's --type
  mode=dark          Material You: dark, light or auto

A file you edited by hand is left alone: the drawer CSS, fuzzel colors,
Strata theme and fastfetch colors are only rewritten while they still hold Perihelion's defaults
or this script's own output. Turning off "Match the wallpaper" in Simpbar
Config (auto_theme "manual") stops all of it.

Usage:
  perihelion-theme                 theme from the current wallpaper
  perihelion-theme IMAGE           theme from IMAGE
  perihelion-theme --color '#RRGGBB'
  options: --style catppuccin|material  --flavor F  --accent wallpaper|flavor
           --scheme TYPE  --force  --dry-run (print
           the chosen palette as JSON, write nothing)
"""

